@page "/vek/community/getting-help"

<DocsPage DisplayFooter="true">
    <DocsPageHeader Title="Getting Help" SubTitle="" />
    <DocsPageContent>
        <DocsPageSection>
            <SectionHeader Title="Let's work through it together.">
                <Description>
                    Stuck while building with Vek? Start a conversation with the community in our <VekLink Href="https://discord.gg/vek">Discord server</VekLink> or post a question in <VekLink Href="https://github.com/madiseh/vek/discussions">GitHub Discussions</VekLink>. A focused question with a small example makes it much easier for others to understand what is happening and suggest a useful next step.
                    <br/><br/>
                    Before posting, take a quick look through the documentation and search existing discussions. If you still need a hand, include the details that help someone reproduce the issue:
                    <br/><br/>
                    <div class="d-flex flex-column px-2">
                        <VekBadge Class="mt-1" Color="Color.Primary" Dot="true" Origin="Origin.CenterLeft">
                            <div class="pl-4 docs-line-height-normal">
                                Describe what you are trying to build and what you expected Vek to do.
                            </div>
                        </VekBadge>
                        <VekBadge Class="mt-1" Color="Color.Primary" Dot="true" Origin="Origin.CenterLeft">
                            <div class="pl-4 docs-line-height-normal">
                                Explain what happened instead, including any error message or unexpected result.
                            </div>
                        </VekBadge>
                        <VekBadge Class="mt-1" Color="Color.Primary" Dot="true" Origin="Origin.CenterLeft">
                            <div class="pl-4 docs-line-height-normal">
                                Share a minimal <VekLink Href="https://github.com/madiseh/vek/snippet" Target="_blank">TryVek</VekLink> example that shows the issue. Remove unrelated code and use sample data where possible.
                            </div>
                        </VekBadge>
                        <VekBadge Class="mt-1" Color="Color.Primary" Dot="true" Origin="Origin.CenterLeft">
                            <div class="pl-4 docs-line-height-normal">
                                Add your Vek and .NET versions, plus the steps you have already tried.
                            </div>
                        </VekBadge>
                    </div>
                    <br/>
                    Keep credentials, private data, and other sensitive information out of examples and screenshots. Once you have posted, stay available for follow-up questions; a little extra context can help the community get you to a solution faster.
                </Description>
            </SectionHeader>
        </DocsPageSection>
    </DocsPageContent>
</DocsPage>
